course: dictionary
lesson: 13098
title: Fishy: smell, suspicion and scams
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Fishy» is an adjective, so it describes a noun. Its first meaning is about smell or taste: «The fish on the plate smelled fishy, so Dad threw it away.» Fish that is not fresh can smell fishy.
explain: The informal meaning is different. «Something fishy is going on» means something seems wrong, or someone is not telling the truth. Look at the clues around the word. If a story has secrets, lies or a sudden strange change, then fishy means suspicious. Try the swap: "something suspicious is going on" still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with fishy when it is about people or messages online. A «fishy» message that asks for your password may be a scam. Context tells you it is a warning, not a smell.
fact: «Fishy» means smelling or tasting of fish.
fact: In an informal way, «fishy» means suspicious, as if something is wrong.
fact: «Something fishy is going on» means something is not right.
fact: A «fishy» message online may be a scam, so tell a grown-up before you reply.
exercise: «The fish on the plate smelled fishy, so Dad threw it away.» What does fishy mean here? | Sweet and sugary | *Smelling of fish, and not fresh | Very cold to touch | Loud and noisy
exercise: «When the money vanished, the teacher said, "Something fishy is going on."» What does fishy mean? | Full of water | Happy and full of fun | *Suspicious, as if something is wrong | Very hot
exercise: Which word can fishy describe in «a fishy ___»? | *smell | quickly | jump | run
test: «Ben's story changed three times, and his voice shook. Something seems fishy.» What does fishy mean? | *Suspicious, as if he is not telling the truth | Very fast | Happy and calm | Covered in scales like a fish
test: «An email said, "You have won a prize, send your password now!" It felt fishy, so Mum deleted it.» What does fishy suggest here? | A fishing trip | *A possible scam, so be careful | A tasty meal | A sunny day at the beach
exam: Which word is a good swap for fishy in «something fishy is going on»? | fishing | tasty | delicious | *suspicious
